  ('analysis', 'analysis.readiness_materializer.valid_window_hours', 'exact', 'int', '24', 'Backstop TTL (hours) for a materialized readiness row''s valid_until (feature 180); the authoritative freshness bust is the bar_epoch-aware FAST gate, so this is only a floor. readiness_valid_until clamps to a 1h minimum. Bounds [1,168].', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_run; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_materialize_readiness_for_owner', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.composite_shrinkage_k', 'exact', 'float', '1', 'Empirical-Bayes pseudo-count `k` for the per-opportunity `composite_score` fusion `(Σwᵢ·sᵢ + 0.5·k)/(Σwᵢ + k)` (feature 199). Deliberately **distinct** from `shrinkage_days` (feature-065 grade, `k` in trading-days): here `k` is dimensionless and equals one axis-weight, so a single maxed axis lands at `0.750` and a corroborated pair at `0.833` (usable `[0.167, 0.833]` band). A configured `0` is honoured (it disables shrinkage). Not seeded by a config-ui migration (code-default only, like the sibling `analysis.scoring.*` keys).', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_retry_unavailable_symbols; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.composite_weight_readiness', 'exact', 'float', '1', 'Fusion weight `wᵢ` for the readiness sub-score (identity map of `conviction`) in the `composite_score` blend (feature 199). A configured `0` is honoured: it disables the readiness axis (its weight is omitted, never a zero score). Code-default only (not config-ui-seeded).', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_retry_unavailable_symbols; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.composite_weight_signal', 'exact', 'float', '1', 'Fusion weight `wᵢ` for the directional-signal sub-score (`clamp(max_agree)·(1−clamp(max_conflict))`) in the `composite_score` blend (feature 199). A configured `0` is honoured: it disables the signal axis. Code-default only (not config-ui-seeded).', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_retry_unavailable_symbols; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.drawdown_weight', 'exact', 'float', '0.3', 'Weight of max drawdown', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_run_backtest; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.min_evidence_days', 'exact', 'int', '500', 'Below this many total evidence trading-days the derived grade is flagged `provisional`.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.min_evidence_symbols', 'exact', 'int', '3', 'Below this many distinct evidence symbols the derived grade is flagged `provisional`.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.sharpe_weight', 'exact', 'float', '0.4', 'Weight of Sharpe in overall score', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_run_backtest; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.shrinkage_days', 'exact', 'int', '250', 'Empirical-Bayes shrinkage pseudo-count `k` (in trading days) for the derived headline grade (feature 065); larger `k` → stronger pull toward the neutral 0.5 prior, so a strong grade needs more evidence. Formula is ANALYSIS-2 in `docs/context-constitution.md`. Read via `int_positive`: a stored ≤ 0 reads as the default 250.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.signal_decay_half_life_hours', 'exact', 'float', '24', 'Exponential half-life (hours) for age decay of a signal''s contribution to the Opportunities queue''s `signal_axis` (feature 022); `effective = conviction × source_weight × exp(−ln2/half_life × age_hours)`, age from `ExternalSignal.ingested_at`. **Registered as a config key with server-enforced bounds `[0, 8760]` (feature 161, migration 019 + config-service `SCALAR_BOUNDS_REGISTRY`)** — appears in config-ui with a bounds hint and is settable via `set_config`. Set to `0` to disable decay (min inclusive); the config service rejects a value outside `[0, 8760]` at `SetConfig` (negative values are no longer settable via `SetConfig`, though the reader still tolerates them defensively). A configured `0` is honoured.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_retry_unavailable_symbols; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.strategy_weight_floor', 'exact', 'float', '0.5', 'Affine grade-weight floor for `strategy_weight = floor + (1−floor)·clamp01(overall_score)` (feature 200); also the neutral weight for a provisional / absent / unattributed grade — never `0`, so an unproven strategy''s opportunity still contributes a term (FR-4/`@AC-7`). A configured `0` is honoured. Code-default only (not config-ui-seeded).', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_strategy_row; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.symbol_score_decay', 'exact', 'float', '0.5', 'Geometric rank-decay γ for the feature-200 symbol_score fold `Σ γ^i·(composite_score × strategy_weight)` (terms sorted DESC). **Read-clamped to `[0, 0.99]`** in `_compute_opportunities` and the heal re-fold — a configured γ≥1 stops the decay / inverts the `@AC-3` saturation ordering. A configured `0` is honoured (it collapses the fold to the top term). Code-default only (not config-ui-seeded), like the sibling `analysis.scoring.*` keys.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_strategy_row; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_compute_opportunities', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.scoring.win_rate_weight', 'exact', 'float', '0.3', 'Weight of win rate', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_run_backtest; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_derive_score_from_cells', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.screener.default_rank_limit', 'exact', 'int', '50', 'Default number of ranked results returned when the request omits `rank_limit`', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/services/screener.py:_rank', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.screener.max_concurrent_formula_evals', 'exact', 'int', '4', 'Max concurrent `ExecuteFormula` evaluations during a scan (semaphore-bounded so a scan can''t starve the live loop)', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/services/screener.py:__init__', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.screener.max_duration_seconds', 'exact', 'int', '120', 'Overall deadline for one screener scan', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:ScreenSymbols', false),
