  ('analysis', 'analysis.strategy.default_cooldown_days', 'exact', 'int', '31', 'Per-strategy default re-entry cooldown in calendar days when `StrategyDefinition.cooldown_days` is unset (feature 069); `31` sits outside the IRS 30-day-each-side wash-sale window. Read via `int_positive`: a platform-wide stored ≤ 0 reads as the default `31` — a per-strategy explicit-`0` (no cooldown) is unaffected because it travels via proto explicit presence, not this config read.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:default_cooldown_days', false),
  ('analysis', 'analysis.strategy.default_exit_cooldown_days', 'exact', 'int', '0', 'Per-strategy default minimum holding period (calendar days) before `exit_rule` may fire a sell, when `StrategyDefinition.exit_cooldown_days` is unset (feature 116); mirrors `default_cooldown_days` but gates the exit transition. Default `0` (no minimum hold — no wash-sale-style rationale exists for a non-zero default here, unlike the 31-day re-entry default). A configured `0` is a legitimate value and is honoured.', 'xstockstrat-analysis', false, 'services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/engine/live_loop.py:_eval_pair; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_run_backtest; services/xstockstrat-analysis/app/handlers/servicer.py:_core', false),
